          "content": {
            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "size": 21242,
            "text": "{\"messages\":{\"secret:pear_bottle_title\":\"Claude Code, now in Desktop preview\",\"secret:pear_bottle_description\":\"Build features, fix bugs, and prototype right in your codebase\",\"secret:copper_oak_trunk\":\"Worktree location\",\"secret:silver_birch_root\":\"Where to store git worktrees for isolated coding sessions\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_title\":\"Trust this workspace?\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_desc\":\"Claude Code may read, write, or execute files in this directory. Only proceed if you trust this workspace.\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_security\":\"Read our <securityLink>security guide</securityLink> for more information.\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_sources\":\"Execution allowed by:\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_cancel\":\"Cancel\",\"secret:rusty_anchor_trust_accept\":\"Trust Workspace\",\"secret:crystal_muffin_bicycle\":\"This artifact requires these connections to work fully. Anthropic can’t guarantee third-party integrations. Use at your own risk.\",\"secret:penguin_tomato_umbrella\":\"This artifact requires specific connections to fulfill its full potential. Review what you’re comfortable sharing with Claude.\",\"secret:wizard_banana_telescope\":\"Enable artifact connectors\",\"secret:rainbow_pickle_harmonica\":\"Let team members work with artifacts that use data from external sources. \",\"secret:disco_ferret_saxophone\":\"Learn more\",\"secret:velvet_pancake_thunder\":\"When Can We Meet?\",\"secret:crimson_butterfly_ocean\":\"Let Claude be your Executive Assistant and find a time when everyone can meet\",\"secret:golden_pickle_symphony\":\"I want to create a react artifact called When Can We Meet? UX: A text area for entering the email addresses of the people you want to meet A drop down for selecting meeting length (15 mins, 30 mins, 45 mins, 60 mins, 75 mins, 90 mins, 105 mins, 120 mins). Working hours with a start time and end time. It should be defaulted to 9am to 5pm. Show times in AM/PM Beautiful professionally designed with white background, blue buttons. It would meet the design standards of Airbnb, Facebook, etc. Show a spinning loading state while you’re waiting for the API response. After results have been fetched show slots in chronological order. Open slots should be green if there are no conflict, and slots with a potentially movable conflict should be yellow and also display the title of the calendar event that may be movable. Include a debug panel that show the raw full contents of the last API response received. Functionality: This artifact uses the Claude API and the Google Calendar MCP to fetch the meetings on the calendars of everyone listed for the next week. MAKE SURE to make a separate API call for each individual’s calendar and fetch everyone’s calendars in parallel. Make sure you track the state of the calls for each person and wait until you’ve received everyone’s calendars before trying to find open slots. After fetching everyone’s calendar, in javascript parse the JSON and then process the events on the calendar using the following rules: If eventType = ‘workingLocation’ then delete this event. If there is an attendees field on the calendar event, then go through the list remove any attendees if the email field ends in ‘@resource.calendar.google.com’. Finally add a ‘may_be_movable’ boolean to each event. may_be_movable should true if A) numAttendees = 2 or B) the phrase ‘focus time’ appears in the event title or C) the attendees field exists and attendees.length = 2. Otherwise may_be_movable is false. Then using javascript it tries to find if there is an overlapping open spot for the selected meeting length that doesn’t require scheduling over an event tagged with ‘may_be_movable’. Then try to find open spots for the selected meeting length if you ignore events tagged with ‘may_be_movable’. The times should be during the specified working hours and should be during the work week (Monday to Friday). Display the first 10 meeting times you find in chronological order. If there are no conflicts show it with a green tag indicating everyone is free. If the slot required scheduling over a meeting tagged with ‘may_be_movable’ show a yellow tag indicating ‘possible conflict’ and display the meeting name whose calendar it appeared on (and be aware there could be multiple conflicts that need to be displayed). DO NOT have a sample response. Make the call to the API and return the real results. If there is an error from the API, show the error. If the API call has a stop_reason of max_tokens or pause_turn, then continue the API call to get the final result and remember to include the full context\",\"secret:marble_cactus_rainbow\":\"Email Reply Drafter\",\"secret:turquoise_waffle_mountain\":\"Save time by using AI to sift through your inbox and draft quick replies to emails\",\"secret:bronze_umbrella_whisper\":\"I want to create a react artifact called Email Reply Drafter. UX: Beautiful professionally designed with white background, blue buttons. It would meet the design standards of Airbnb, Facebook, etc. Have a debug panel that shows the raw response from the last API call. Functionality: Using the Claude API and the Gmail MCP, fetch the users 50 most recent conversations from their inbox when they load the page. Filter out anything that looks like it doesn’t need a reply (newsletters, spam, the user is already the last one to reply on the thread etc) and then display the set of emails that potentially need replies. The emails should be displayed in an inbox style format where you see the sender and subject line and the user can click in to view the actual contents. Make sure to save the threadId for each email, since you will need it later. When a user clicks into a email, have a text area called Brief Reply Instructions where they can write some brief notes on what the reply should be. There should be a button Draft Reply that they can click. When they click Draft Reply make a call to the Claude API to draft an email reply based on the instructions the user input. Display the draft to the user and let them make edits. The user can edit the reply and then there is a Save button for the user to save the email draft. If the users clicks Save then make a call to the Claude API and Gmail MCP to save the email as a draft. Make sure to pass threadId when you make the call to save the draft so the reply is within the original email thread. Once they have saved a draft, show a widget at the bottom that shows a count of the total number of drafts a user has saved along with a link Send Drafts that links to https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#drafts\",\"secret:silver_donut_carnival\":\"Contact Email History Analyzer\",\"secret:amber_sandwich_nebula\":\"Transform email threads into organized summaries with key topics, action items, and conversation timeline\",\"secret:copper_banana_fortress\":\"Create a React Contact Email Analyzer that helps users review their email history with specific contacts, using the Gmail MCP in the artifact. Main Features: - Email input field and time period selector (Past Week, Month, 3 Months, 6 Months, Year) - Default to Past Month - Search Gmail for emails to/from that contact in the selected timeframe - Generate a summary showing: total conversations, timeline of emails, main topics discussed, and action items - Save the last 10 searches so users can quickly re-run them What to Display: - Overview section with total email count - Timeline showing email dates, subjects, and previews - Key Topics as clickable tags - Action Items as a simple list - Search history dropdown when clicking the email field\",\"secret:velvet_cupcake_spark\":\"This artifact wants to access shared data that other users of this artifact can see. You might see unverified content from others, and any data you save will be visible to them. Make sure you aren’t sharing sensitive information.\",\"secret:silver_apple_jungle\":\"Clear storage\",\"secret:golden_pear_forest\":\"Are you sure you want to clear the storage? This will delete all the data you have in this artifact and can’t be recovered. Shared artifacts won’t be affected.\",\"secret:cotton_camel_pyramid\":\"Failed to clear storage. Please try again.\",\"secret:sew_ball_disco\":\"Piloting Claude for Chrome\",\"secret:random_mountain_band\":\"Now Claude can navigate, click buttons, and fill forms—right in your browser. Max users get early access to test, explore, and shape what’s next.\",\"secret:quantum_rabbit_telescope\":\"Claude for Chrome\",\"secret:cosmic_butterfly_piano\":\"Try Claude for Chrome\",\"secret:open_pelican_water\":\"Add to Chrome\",\"secret:golden_bridge_adventure\":\"Meet Claude for Chrome\",\"secret:velvet_moon_safari\":\"When AI can interact with web pages, it creates meaningful value, but also opens up new risks. We’re releasing\",\"secret:crystal_star_journey\":\"as a limited research preview to learn from real-world use.\",\"secret:mystic_ocean_harmony\":\"Our goal is to explore safe ways for AI to browse the web—not just for our products, but for the entire AI ecosystem.\",\"secret:compostable_centric_milk\":\"Install the Claude browser extension, and ask it to:\",\"secret:projection_pineapple_cloth\":\"Claude’s in your Chrome\",\"secret:fabric_research_panther\":\"Claude won’t work perfectly or risk-free on all websites or tasks.\",\"secret:phone_pillow_sleep\":\"Get familiar with the browser extension before surfing the world wide web.\",\"secret:brother_rolling_wire\":\"Ready to roam Chrome?\",\"secret:velvet_telescope_pizza\":\"I’m a Max plan subscriber. When do I get access?\",\"secret:banana_thunder_violin\":\"What shouldn’t I use this for?\",\"secret:jellyfish_waffle_lamp\":\"How do I control what Claude can access?\",\"secret:cinnamon_bicycle_moon\":\"What are the security risks I should know about?\",\"secret:penguin_whistle_taco\":\"When will other Claude plans get access?\",\"secret:marmalade_sock_galaxy\":\"We’re starting with 1,000 Max users and expanding gradually based on what we learn. Join the research preview waitlist and we’ll notify you when your access is ready, along with installation instructions and safety guidelines.\",\"secret:origami_doorknob_fog\":\"Avoid financial transactions, password management, or anything involving sensitive personal data. Start with trusted sites and familiar workflows where you’re comfortable having Claude take actions. Never use it for high-stakes decisions without careful supervision. And, of course, make sure your use complies with our\",\"secret:origami_doorknob_fog_link\":\"acceptable use policy\",\"secret:bubblegum_anchor_nest\":\"You decide which websites Claude can visit and what actions it can take. Claude asks permission before visiting new sites and before taking potentially risky actions like publishing content or making purchases. You can revoke access to specific websites anytime in settings. For trusted workflows, you can choose to skip all permissions, but you should supervise Claude closely. While some safeguards exist for sensitive actions, malicious actors could still trick Claude into unintended actions.\",\"secret:kaleidoscope_pretzel_cave\":\"Browser AI faces unique security risks, like prompt injection attacks, where malicious actors might try to trick Claude into unintended actions, such as sharing your bank information or deleting important files. While we’ve implemented protections, they aren’t full proof. Attack vectors are constantly evolving and Claude may hallucinate, leading to actions that you did not intend. We’ve shared our testing results, including possible attack scenarios, so you can make informed decisions, and strongly encourage you to\",\"secret:kaleidoscope_pretzel_cave_link\":\"read about the risks\",\"secret:kaleidoscope_pretzel_cave_end\":\"before using this product.\",\"secret:marshmallow_compass_yeti\":\"We’re focused on learning from Max plan users first during this experimental phase. As we improve safety and reliability based on real usage, we’ll gradually expand to other plans. Our timeline depends on what we discover during research preview.\",\"secret:cosmic_keyboard_mountain\":\"Unsubscribe from unwanted email chains\",\"secret:mystic_dolphin_harmonica\":\"Find apartments matching preferences\",\"secret:electric_pancake_wizard\":\"Extract and summarize key insights\",\"secret:velvet_thunder_butterfly\":\"Please help me unsubscribe from all promotional emails in my inbox that I haven’t opened in the last 3 months.\",\"secret:crystal_moonlight_pickle\":\"I’m looking for a 3-bedroom house in Seattle under $800K, with a garage and at least 1500sqft. Can you search Zillow and show me the top 5 options?\",\"secret:rainbow_telescope_dragon\":\"Can you analyze these meeting notes and extract the key action items and deadlines into a structured summary?\",\"secret:lunar_sandwich_telescope\":\"Help us build what’s next\",\"secret:cosmic_jelly_mountain\":\"Using this feature and giving feedback directly improves what Claude can do.\",\"secret:mystic_pretzel_ocean\":\"This is a Google extension. The use of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.\",\"secret:thunder_cookie_telescope\":\"Understand the risks\",\"secret:crystal_waffle_butterfly\":\"Claude brings AI directly to your browser, handling tasks and navigating sites for you. These new capabilities create risks bad actors may try to exploit.\",\"secret:velvet_pancake_harmonica\":\"Malicious actors can hide instructions in websites, emails, and documents that trick AI into taking harmful actions without your knowledge, including:\",\"secret:electric_muffin_dragon\":\"Accessing your accounts or files\",\"secret:rainbow_pickle_wizard\":\"Sharing your private information\",\"secret:cosmic_donut_mountain\":\"Making purchases on your behalf\",\"secret:mystic_cookie_ocean\":\"Taking actions you never intended\",\"secret:lunar_jelly_telescope\":\"Learn more about the risks\",\"secret:thunder_waffle_butterfly\":\"Read the blogpost\",\"secret:crystal_pretzel_harmonica\":\"How to browse safely\",\"secret:velvet_muffin_dragon\":\"This beta experience is designed for AI-experienced users who understand these safety measures.\",\"secret:electric_pickle_wizard\":\"Start with trusted sites\",\"secret:rainbow_donut_mountain\":\"Only grant permissions to familiar websites while you’re learning how Claude works.\",\"secret:quantum_browser_tornado\":\"The browser extension is a beta feature with unique risks—stay alert and protect yourself from bad actors.\",\"secret:saturn_cupcake_violin\":\"Review before sensitive actions\",\"secret:jupiter_brownie_guitar\":\"Always confirm before Claude handles financial, personal, or work-critical tasks.\",\"secret:neptune_cookie_piano\":\"Watch for malicious instructions\",\"secret:mercury_muffin_drums\":\"Be cautious if Claude behaves unexpectedly—some sites hide instructions to override yours.\",\"secret:venus_cake_flute\":\"Report issues immediately\",\"secret:mars_pastry_harp\":\"Help us improve by flagging any concerning behavior through the feedback options.\",\"secret:golden_butterfly_mountain\":\"Understand the risks\",\"secret:bogosort_push_notif_subtitle\":\"Get notified when Claude has finished a response. Most useful for long-running tasks like tool calls, Research, and Claude Code on the web.\",\"secret:bogosort_email_notif_title\":\"Emails from Claude Code on the web\",\"secret:bogosort_email_notif_subtitle\":\"Get an email when Claude Code on the web has finished building or needs your response.\",\"secret:frozen_penguin_avalanche\":\"Get Claude for Chrome\",\"secret:arctic_polar_snowstorm\":\"Exclusive access for Max plan subscribers\",\"secret:twilight_cavern_sunrise\":\"Coming soon for Teams and Enterprise\",\"secret:crystal_glacier_twilight\":\"Claude for Chrome is currently only available for Max plan subscribers. We're working on expanding access.\",\"secret:bronze_river_valley\":\"Your Sonnet usage counts toward this limit, as well as your weekly and 5-hour session limits\",\"secret:golden_lake_forest\":\"You haven't used Sonnet yet\",\"secret:emerald_tide_whisper\":\"Sonnet only\",\"secret:arctic_seal_title\":\"Fast mode\",\"secret:arctic_seal_badge\":\"Research preview\",\"secret:arctic_seal_subtitle\":\"Allow your team to use fast mode. Fast mode has the same intelligence with significantly faster output. It uses more credits and is billed via extra usage.\",\"secret:arctic_seal_error\":\"Failed to update fast mode setting. You can try again.\",\"secret:arctic_seal_free_disabled\":\"Fast mode is not available in the free plan.\",\"secret:arctic_seal_extra_usage_link\":\"Extra usage must be enabled for fast mode to work. Please enable extra usage and set limits under <link>Usage</link>.\",\"secret:arctic_seal_usage_notice\":\"Fast mode respects spend limits set.\",\"secret:cobalt_wave_title\":\"Remote Control\",\"secret:cobalt_wave_badge\":\"Research preview\",\"secret:cobalt_wave_subtitle\":\"Allow your team to continue local Claude Code sessions from claude.ai/code or the Claude mobile app. Sessions run on the user's machine with full access to their local filesystem, tools, and project configuration. <link>Learn more</link>\",\"secret:cobalt_wave_error\":\"Failed to update Remote Control setting. You can try again.\",\"secret:cobalt_wave_policy_blocked\":\"Your organization's policies don't allow changing this setting.\",\"secret:hollow_lantern_title\":\"Allow auto permissions mode\",\"secret:hollow_lantern_subtitle\":\"Auto mode lets Claude handle permission decisions during coding sessions, so developers can run longer tasks without being interrupted by Claude asking for manual approvals. Auto mode also includes additional safeguards against prompt injections.\",\"secret:hollow_lantern_policy_blocked\":\"Your organization's policies don't allow changing this setting.\",\"secret:hollow_lantern_error\":\"Failed to update auto permissions setting. You can try again.\",\"secret:willow_quarry_bend\":\"File size exceeds {maxSizeMB}MB limit. Choose a smaller file.\",\"secret:copper_fern_basin\":\"Invalid file type. Only PNG, JPEG, and WebP images are allowed.\",\"secret:amber_brook_glade\":\"Logo\",\"secret:slate_ember_ridge\":\"Remove icon\",\"secret:ember_quill_mark\":\"Claude\",\"secret:amber_scroll_seal\":\"Accepted\",\"secret:copper_ink_trace\":\"Suggestion:\",\"secret:silver_quill_tip\":\"Accept suggestion\",\"secret:bronze_scroll_end\":\"Remove comment\",\"secret:iron_quill_press\":\"Review code\",\"secret:slate_bell_chime\":\"Code review complete\",\"secret:oak_leaf_drift\":\"No issues found.\",\"secret:pine_bell_ring\":\"{count, plural, one {# comment to review.} other {# comments to review.}}\",\"secret:birch_leaf_clear\":\"Code review complete — no issues found.\",\"secret:maple_bell_note\":\"Code review complete — {count, plural, one {# comment} other {# comments}} to review.\",\"secret:iron_anvil_hero_label\":\"Actual tokens served from cache. May be lower than billed due to cache evictions or block rounding (1,024 or 4,096 tokens depending on hardware).\",\"secret:iron_anvil_billed_tooltip\":\"Billed (expected): tokens the API predicted would cache-hit before inference. Actual: tokens actually served from cache. Difference from cache evictions or block rounding.\",\"secret:velvet_compass_desc\":\"Have a coupon? Enter it below to extend your Max 20x subscription.\",\"secret:velvet_compass_input_label\":\"Coupon code\",\"secret:velvet_compass_input_placeholder\":\"Enter code\",\"secret:velvet_compass_check\":\"Check\",\"secret:velvet_compass_apply\":\"Apply coupon\",\"secret:velvet_compass_success\":\"Coupon applied\",\"secret:velvet_compass_error_invalid\":\"That coupon code isn't valid. Check the code and try again.\",\"secret:saffron_port_section_title\":\"Import memory from other AI providers\",\"secret:saffron_port_section_description\":\"Bring relevant context and data from another AI provider to Claude. We'll provide a prompt you can use to fetch the memory from your other account.\",\"secret:saffron_port_button\":\"Start import\",\"secret:saffron_port_title\":\"Import memory to Claude\",\"secret:saffron_port_prompt_label\":\"Copy this prompt into a chat with your other AI provider\",\"secret:saffron_port_input_label\":\"Paste results below to add to Claude's memory\",\"secret:saffron_port_input_placeholder\":\"Paste your memory details here\",\"secret:saffron_port_copy\":\"Copy prompt\",\"secret:saffron_port_copy_label\":\"Copy\",\"secret:saffron_port_submit\":\"Add to memory\",\"secret:saffron_port_cancel\":\"Cancel\",\"secret:saffron_port_learn_more\":\"Learn more\",\"secret:saffron_port_see_in_action\":\"See what Claude learned about you\",\"secret:saffron_port_memory_updated_label\":\"Memory updated\",\"secret:saffron_port_memory_updated_toast\":\"Memory updated!\",\"secret:amber_reef_cancel\":\"Cancel anytime\",\"secret:amber_reef_no_commitment\":\"No commitment \\\\u00b7 Cancel anytime\",\"secret:cobalt_wrench_title\":\"Integration permissions\",\"secret:conductor_admin_toggle_title\":\"Let Claude work across apps\",\"secret:conductor_admin_toggle_description\":\"Members can let Claude share context between apps like Excel and PowerPoint.\"},\"gates\":[\"chilling_sloth\",\"claude_create_marble\",\"claude_create_pebble_stone\",\"claude_ai_crochet\",\"curse_you_perry_the_platypus\",\"igloo_hurricane_blizzard\",\"moonlight_stalagmite_raspberry\",\"prism_vault_echo\",\"claudeai_claude_code_penguin_mode_admin\",\"tengu_ccr_bridge_org_toggle\",\"tengu_hollow_lantern\",\"crooked_sundial\",\"ccr_once_over\",\"cache_scoped_prompt_ordering\",\"max_20x_extension_coupon\",\"claudeai_saffron_port_enabled\",\"risk_reversal_microcopy\",\"pivot_hive_web\"],\"locale\":\"en-US\"}"
          },
